            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0203" n="103" xml:id="pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1193: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-01T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Your 73, October 21, 8 am.</p>
                <p>Department approves the attitude of the Financial Adviser in stating to the
                    manager of the Bank of British West Africa that an attempt of the Liberian
                    Government to raise a loan without first consulting with him would be a
                    violation of the provisions of the Reform Program and the 1912 Agreement. Should
                    the Department subsequently agree to receive the proposed commission, the
                    Financial Adviser should then approve loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
